# Updating project & task management plans

When you add, change, or ship **project tasks**, **project detail**, **Kanban**, or related `project_tasks` behaviour, update **Dira** workspace `foro` (MCP `dira`). Do not recreate git `docs/`.

## 1. Rolling progress log (required)

Edit **`docs/web/plans/project-task-management/progress.md`**:

- Bump the **Last reviewed** date if material work changed.
- Update the **Summary** table (phase status: Done / Mostly done / Not started / Planning).
- Add a **Changelog** bullet with date: what shipped or what gap was closed.
- Adjust **Next actions** so the queue matches reality.

## 2. Phase spec checklists (required when a phase moves)

Open the matching **`docs/web/plans/project-task-management/phase-*.md`** file(s):

- Set **`Status:`** line at the top (e.g. Done, Mostly done, Not started).
- Tick **`[x]`** / leave **`[ ]`** on deliverables to match the codebase.
- If scope moved (e.g. list + board shipped on one page), say so in the phase doc so the written plan matches implementation.

## 3. Hub and indexes (when scope or status shifts)

- **`docs/web/plans/project-task-management/readme.md`** — phase table **Status** column should match PROGRESS.
- **`docs/web/plans/readme.md`** — keep the row pointing at the hub + progress log accurate.
- **`docs/web/readme.md`** — if new module docs were added, link them.

## 4. Schema and module docs (when DB or API contract changes)

- **`docs/web/03-database/project-tasks-schema-contract.md`** — update when columns, constraints, or indexes change; verify with MySQL MCP (`mysql_describe_table`) before editing shapes.
- **`docs/web/02-modules/project-tasks.md`** — routes, UI entry points, and service overview.
- **`docs/api/api.md` / `docs/api/database.md`** — if the HTTP or MySQL contract changed.

## 5. Do not edit by default

- Do **not** change **`docs/web/plans/readme.md`** vision sections (long roadmap narrative) unless the product vision itself changed.
- Do **not** edit auto-generated **`.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`** snapshot files from the IDE; the source of truth is Dira **`docs/web/plans/project-task-management/`**.

## Quick checklist before merging PM work

- [ ] Dira PROGRESS updated (summary + changelog).
- [ ] Relevant `phase-*.md` deliverables / status lines updated.
- [ ] Hub README phase table aligned.
- [ ] Schema or `docs/web/02-modules/project-tasks.md` touched if behaviour or routes changed.
